      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0051",
      "sequence": 906,
      "meaning": "Seeing the army in distress, Hanumān rushes like angry Time, uproots a great mountain and hurls it at Meghanāda. Indrajit escapes into the sky, but chariot, horses and driver are destroyed. Hanumān repeatedly challenges him, yet he knows the secret and will not approach. Indrajit goes near Rāma, abuses him and casts every missile and weapon, which the Lord cuts away as play. Frustrated by that power, the fool uses many illusions—like one trying to frighten Garuḍa by holding a tiny snake—and shows his defective magic to the very Lord whose mighty māyā controls Śiva and Brahmā.",
