    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0052",
      "sequence": 907,
      "meaning": "From the sky Indrajit rains coals while streams of water spring from earth. Dancing male and female spirits cry ‘kill, cut’; filth, pus, blood, hair and bones rain down, then stones and dense dust spread darkness until one cannot see an outstretched hand. The monkeys panic, certain death has arrived. Rāma smiles at the spectacle, recognizing their fear, and one arrow cuts away the whole illusion as the sun disperses darkness. His gracious gaze makes bears and monkeys unstoppable again. With Aṅgada and the others, angry Lakṣmaṇa takes bow and arrows and seeks Rāma’s leave for battle.",
