      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0053",
      "sequence": 908,
      "meaning": "Lakṣmaṇa’s red eyes, broad chest and arms and snow-mountain body tinged red are seen as Rāvaṇa sends many armed champions. Monkeys carrying mountains, claws and trees rush crying victory to Rāma, and evenly matched warriors clash with intense desire for victory. With fists, kicks and teeth the victorious monkeys tear foes, rebuke them, wrench off heads and arms and fill the nine regions with cries of ‘strike’ and ‘seize.’ Headless trunks run everywhere while gods watch from the sky in alternating wonder and joy. Trenches fill and clot with blood, dust rising above them like smoke over heaps of coals.",
