      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0054",
      "sequence": 909,
      "meaning": "Wounded heroes shine like flowering kiṃśuka trees. Lakṣmaṇa and Meghanāda fight furiously, neither able to defeat the other, while the demon uses deceit. Enraged Lakṣmaṇa quickly smashes chariot and driver and attacks in many ways until Rāvaṇa’s son is barely alive. Realizing his life is in danger, Indrajit releases the hero-killing śakti. It strikes the radiant Lakṣmaṇa’s chest and he falls unconscious. Indrajit approaches without fear, but even hundreds of millions like him cannot lift the cosmic support Śeṣa; humiliated, they depart.",
