      "sequence": 910,
      "meaning": "Śiva says Lakṣmaṇa’s fire of anger could instantly consume the fourteen worlds—who could conquer him while gods, humans and creation serve him? Only one graced by Rāma knows this play. At evening both armies withdraw to tend their own forces. The all-pervading, unborn, unconquered Lord asks where Lakṣmaṇa is; Hanumān carries him in, and Rāma grieves at his brother’s condition. Jāmbavān names the physician Suṣeṇa in Laṅkā. Hanumān assumes a tiny form and swiftly brings physician and house together. Bowing to Rāma, Suṣeṇa names the mountain and herb Hanumān must fetch.",
