    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0056",
      "sequence": 911,
      "meaning": "Holding Rāma’s lotus feet in his heart, Hanumān departs proclaiming strength. A messenger informs Rāvaṇa, who visits Kālanemi and explains. The demon repeatedly shakes his head: who can block the path of the one who burned the city before Rāvaṇa’s eyes? He urges Rāvaṇa to worship Raghupati for his own welfare, stop false boasting, place the lovely dark lotus-bodied Lord in his heart, abandon ‘I, you and mine,’ and wake from the night of delusion. Can anyone defeat in battle the devourer of the serpent Time? Enraged Rāvaṇa compels him; Kālanemi decides death by Rāma’s envoy is preferable to death at the villain’s hands.",
