    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0057",
      "sequence": 912,
      "meaning": "Kālanemi creates an illusion along the road: pond, temple and fine garden, with himself posed as a sage in a lovely hermitage. Hanumān asks where to drink and relieve fatigue. The disguised demon chants Rāma’s virtues, predicts Rāma’s certain victory, and boasts of seeing it through superior insight. When Hanumān asks for water, he offers a small water-pot; Hanumān says it will not satisfy him. Kālanemi sends him to bathe in the pond and hurry back for initiation into knowledge. Entering, Hanumān’s foot is seized by a crocodile; he kills it, and it assumes a divine body and ascends to heaven.",
