      "meaning": "The freed celestial woman says Hanumān’s sight removed her sin and a great sage’s curse. She warns that the supposed sage is a dreadful demon and asks him to trust her. After she departs, Hanumān approaches Kālanemi and jokingly requests that the guru take his fee before giving the mantra. He wraps his tail around the demon’s head and hurls him down; revealing his body at death, Kālanemi cries Rāma’s name and dies. Hanumān rejoices, reaches the mountain but cannot identify the herb, so uproots the peak and flies through the night. Passing over Ayodhyā, he is mistaken by Bharata for a huge demon and struck by a blunt arrow drawn to the ear.",
