      "sequence": 914,
      "meaning": "Hit by the arrow, Hanumān falls unconscious calling Rāma. Hearing the beloved name, Bharata rushes anxiously to him, embraces the senseless monkey and tries repeatedly to wake him. With darkened face, tear-filled eyes and grief, he says fate that turned him from Rāma has dealt this further cruel blow. If his love for Rāma’s lotus feet is guileless in mind, speech and body, and Raghupati favours him, let the monkey rise free from pain and fatigue. Hearing this, Hanumān sits up crying victory to Kosala’s Lord. Bharata embraces him again, thrilled and tearful, unable to contain love as he remembers Rāma.",
