      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0060",
      "sequence": 915,
      "meaning": "Bharata asks after the treasure of joy, his younger brother and Mother Jānakī. Hanumān briefly recounts everything; Bharata grieves that fate has made him useless to the Lord. Recognizing the urgent hour, he steadies himself and warns that delay will ruin the mission at dawn. He offers to send Hanumān and the mountain upon his arrow to the abode of compassion. Hanumān briefly wonders how an arrow could carry his weight, then remembers Rāma’s power, bows with joined hands and says he will go at once holding Bharata’s majesty in his heart. As he flies, he repeatedly praises Bharata’s arm-strength, character, virtues and limitless love for the Lord’s feet.",
